course: dictionary
lesson: 5536
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word leg can mean different things, so context tells you which meaning is right. «The spider has eight legs.» Here a leg is a part of the body that an animal uses to walk.
explain: «The wobbly table needed a new leg.» A table is not an animal, so leg must mean the part that holds the table up. Ask yourself: what is this leg doing in the sentence?
explain: «The race had three legs, and Mia ran the last one.» Here a leg is one part of a longer trip or race. «He pulled on his trousers, and the leg was torn.» Now it is the part of trousers that covers your leg.
fact: A leg is a part of the body that people and animals stand and walk on.
fact: Tables, chairs and stools have legs that hold them up.
fact: A leg of a trip or a race is one part of it.
fact: Insects have 6 legs, and spiders have 8 legs.
fact: «Break a leg» is a phrase that means good luck, often said to an actor.
exercise: «A hen has two legs, and a dog has four legs.» How many legs does a dog have? | Two | Six | Eight | *Four
exercise: «The stool had three legs, so it wobbled a little.» What are the legs in this sentence? | *Parts that hold the stool up | Parts of a body used for walking | Parts of a race | Parts of trousers
exercise: «The race had three legs, and Mia ran the last one.» What does leg mean here? | The leg of trousers | A spider's leg | A part of the body | *One part of the race
test: «Insects have six legs, but spiders have eight legs.» How many legs does a spider have? | Two | *Eight | Four | Six
test: «The left leg of his trousers was torn.» What does leg mean here? | A leg of a trip or a race | A table leg | A part of the body used for walking | *The part of trousers that covers your leg
exam: «The car hit him and broke his leg.» What is the leg in this sentence? | The leg of his trousers | One part of a race | A table leg | *A part of the body used for walking
